{
  "title": "Bone Tumor Staging Systems",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8001/bone-tumor-staging-systems",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Nov 30 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Prognosis of bone cancer depends on the following variables overall **stage** of disease (incorporates all of the below) presence of **metastasis skip (discontinous) lesions** within the same bone **histologic grade tumor size**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The are two staging systems that are commonly used:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**MSTS or Enneking System**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**AJCC Staging System**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MSTS (Enneking) Staging System",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most popular and useful for orthopaedic surgeons",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "two systems - one for malignant lesions and one for benign lesions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "malignant lesions are defined using Roman numerals (e.g. I, II, III)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "see table below",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "e.g. osteosarcoma most commonly presents as stage IIB",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "benign lesions are defined using Arabic numbers (1,2,3)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**1 = latent lesion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "e.g. non-ossifying fibroma",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "enchondroma",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**2 = active lesion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "e.g. ABC, UBC",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "chondromyxoid fibroma",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "chondroblastoma",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**3 = aggressive lesion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "e.g. giant cell tumor of bone",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "",
              "table": [
